1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,425
How Chess Conquered the World.

2
00:00:02,375 --> 00:00:12,437
Chess originated in 6th-century India as chaturanga, representing four divisions of an army: infantry, cavalry, elephants, and chariots.

3
00:00:12,437 --> 00:00:17,350
The game spread to Persia and subsequently to Europe through Islamic expansion.

4
00:00:17,350 --> 00:00:24,212
The modern game crystallized in 15th-century Spain when the queen and bishop gained their powerful long-range moves.

5
00:00:24,212 --> 00:00:29,100
The first official World Chess Championship was held in 1886.

6
00:00:29,100 --> 00:00:37,537
In 1997, IBM Deep Blue defeated world champion Garry Kasparov, marking a milestone in artificial intelligence.

7
00:00:37,537 --> 00:00:51,125
Online platforms now allow anyone to play opponents globally at any time, and chess has experienced renewed popularity, with millions playing daily on digital platforms and major tournaments streamed live to global audiences.

